  "N18" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: External forces lack control, and equilibrium is elusive, so precise control is missing."];
  "N2" [label="(3,0,0) Single crystals are recognized as an ideal platform to access peak semiconducting performances."];
  "N20" [label="(13,0,0) We introduce a universal nanoconfined molecular-dipole orienting (nano-CMDO) strategy."];
  "N21" [label="(14,0,0) Molecular dipoles rotate conjugated backbones in response to a perpendicular electric field, while plates regulate side chains."];
  "N22" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Nano-CMDO is introduced, and it rotates backbones/regulates chains, so it provides precise control."];
  "N24" [label="(15,0,0) A series of prototype CPs are manufactured into microscale-size high-quantity single-crystal thin films."];
  "N25" [label="(16,0,0) These films exhibit ultralow energetic disorders with the minimal Urbach energy of 25 meV."];
  "N26" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Prototype CPs are manufactured, and films exhibit low disorder, so crystallization is successful."];
  "N27" [label="(17,0,0) Trap-free SCLC behaviors are observed with notably low trap densities."];
  "N28" [label="(18,0,0) A high transistor mobility of 15.5 cm2 V-1 s-1 is achieved."];
  "N29" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Trap-free behaviors observed, and high mobility achieved, so performance is high-quality."];
  "N3" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: CPs are pioneering in electronics, and single crystals access peak performance, so CP single crystals are needed."];
  "N4" [label="(4,0,0) Manufacturing of CP single crystals remains significantly challenging due to energy/entropy contradiction."];
  "N5" [label="(5,0,0) Challenge is exacerbated in thin films due to 2D constraints and disruptions."];
  "N6" [label="(0,0,0) Induction-reasoning: Manufacturing is challenging, and exacerbated in thin films, so thin-film manufacturing is a significant barrier."];
  "N7" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-reasoning: Currently there is a need and a barrier, and if need+barrier then problem, so a research problem exists."];
  "N8" [label="(6,0,0) Electronegativity differences between carbon and heteroatoms create localized molecular dipoles."];
  "N9" [label="(7,0,0) From the thermodynamic perspective, molecular dipoles may serve as subtle modulators to influence the energy landscape."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This paper proposes and evaluates a nanoconfined molecular-dipole orienting strategy based on a spatial-electrostatic nanoconfined capacitor: a perpendicular electric field rotates molecular dipoles in conjugated polymers, while alkyl-modified plates guide side-chain orientation, enabling diverse conjugated polymers to assemble into microscale single-crystal thin films with ultralow energetic disorder and high carrier mobility.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) A strategy that couples field-driven molecular-dipole orientation with nanoscale confinement and side-chain guidance can address CP thin-film crystallization challenges while enabling low-disorder, high-mobility single-crystal films."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Nano-CMDO is a plausible proposed control strategy for the identified crystallization-control challenge because it uses a perpendicular electric field to rotate molecular dipoles and alkyl-modified plates to regulate side-chain orientation."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) The reported nano-CMDO films show successful materials outcomes: prototype conjugated polymers are manufactured into microscale single-crystal thin films with ultralow energetic disorder, and the films also show trap-free behavior with high carrier mobility."];
  "R14" [label="(0,0,0) Nano-CMDO is proposed as a control strategy and is empirically supported by reported crystallization and electronic-performance outcomes."];
  "R15" [label="(0,0,0) Because nano-CMDO is proposed to address the crystallization-control problem and is supported by reported results, it is a promising avenue for fabricating high-quality CP single-crystal thin films."];
  "R16" [label="(0,0,0) Because localized molecular dipoles exist in CPs and are expected to influence the energy landscape and accelerate nucleation, molecular dipoles are a potential lever for CP crystallization."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Accelerated nucleation is often associated with high-density random crystal nuclei that lead to polycrystals, and molecular dipoles are sensitive to molecular configurations and stacking conformations."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) CP crystallization faces control challenges because accelerated nucleation can create random nuclei and polycrystals, while existing external-force alignment lacks nanoscopic control and has not achieved a delicate equilibrium between localized molecular rotations and comprehensive chain alignments."];
